        verification storyControlEventCoverageDoD : Test { :>> id = "6f8cd3ca-a813-476e-a661-d82001570c9d"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "DELIVERED (D0193, accepted on their 'approved. keep the momentum going'): dcEnforcementPointSpecPin, dcActorRebindLedger, dcOverrideCountedOnSuccess - the three per-instance resolvers folded under one control exactly as the decision decrees. (1) control-events.toml declares all 12 control-event classes with their required records and the encoding notes (the actor-rebind transition rides the ledger's decision string; the rationale is IN the contract, not in anyone's head). (2) Guard 45 control-event-coverage (WARNING tier): a two-way diff between the declaration and the event names the binary emits - dead declarations and uncounted events both warn; absent contract reports not-adopted (D0136); first run PASSED with 12 scanned and zero warnings, meaning declaration and emitters matched on day one. (3) issue203: the build-time spec-pin point is now in the enforcementPoints inventory with its warn-allow residual stated. (4) issue205: keel actor set leaves a durable record - VERIFIED LIVE: a real rebind appended {event: actor-rebind, decision: claudeFable5->claudeFable5} and enforcement-report counted it (fires: 1). (5) issue207: the happy-path consumption emits override-consumed; pm counts consumed and unsynced separately, bound by a new unit test (3 overrides / 1 unsynced on a synthetic ledger). guards.md + CLAUDE.md 44 -> 45 same commit."; }
        part storyControlEventCoverageDoDR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "a43196dd-22de-4b23-b55b-623ba04b7213"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "114663c"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-08-21"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
