    verification controlEventCoverageReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "fada45f3-49ed-421e-a4ca-1486264e99a2"; :>> title = "Sprint 407 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-08-22"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "PASS 1, CLAIMS: every verification above is a live run or an executed test quoted from this session's output. PASS 2, BOUNDARY: the guard's EMITTED_LEDGER constant is a hand-maintained list - the exact drift class the guard polices in the contract - so the constant going stale IS caught (a new emitter without the constant shows up as emitted-not-declared only if the contract gains it; a new emitter added nowhere is invisible to the guard). Stated plainly: the two-way diff catches one-sided drift, not both-sided omission; the review discipline for new ledger_emit call sites is the residual, named in the constant's own doc. PASS 3, OWN DIFF: the pm test initially asserted invented field names (overrides/overridesUnsynced) - caught by reading the emitter before running, corrected to the real overrideLedgerEvents/overrideObligationsUnsynced. WHAT A REVIEWER SHOULD ATTACK: the decision-string encoding for rebind transitions - it trades a dedicated field (schema break) for a documented convention; if the ledger schema ever unfreezes, this is the first row to normalize."; }
